<title>USA: Advantage Bancorp to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Advantage Bancorp to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>KENOSHA, Wis. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advantage Bancorp Inc said Monday it will repurchase up to five percent of its common stock outstanding during the six months beginning November 13, 1996.</p>
<p>Advantage, which has total assets of $1.02 billion, said this is its ninth buyback since it became a public company in March 1992.  </p>
<p>Advantage said the shares will be purchased at prevailing market prices from time to time depending upon market conditions.</p>
<p>The company now has about 3,277,000 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The repurchased shares will become treasury shares to be used in connection with the exercise of stock options and other general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
